meta {
  name: Update Lab Test Field Permissions
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/business-admin/lab-test-field-permissions
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "config": {
      "Basic Details": {
        "Department": false
      }
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("Department is now Denied", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().data.config["Basic Details"]["Department"]).to.equal(false);
  });
  test("other Basic Details fields untouched", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().data.config["Basic Details"]["Test Name"]).to.equal(true);
  });
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `business_admin:lab_test_master_setting__update_lab_test_master_setting` — enforced by `PermissionGuard` (`@RequirePermission`). A caller whose effective permissions (user override ?? branch-role override ?? role baseline) lack this get **403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`**; the `business_admin` / `administrator` roles bypass all checks, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` (an admin) still succeeds here.

  Merge the given `config` into the caller's tenant Lab Test Master Setting
  overrides (tenant id taken from JWT) and return the fully-resolved map.

  ## Required fields
  - `config` — `{ [section]: { [field]: boolean } }`. Only the sections/fields
    being changed need to be included — everything else keeps its current
    value. Unknown section/field names and non-boolean values are ignored.

  ## Sections & fields
  `Basic Details`, `Pricing`, `TAT`, `Flags`, `Sample`, `Results`,
  `Reference Range`, `Reference Value`, `Version Control` — see
  `GET Lab Test Field Permissions` for the full field list per section.

  Audited under `AuditModule.LAB_TEST_FIELD_PERMISSIONS`
  (`AuditAction.UPDATE`).
}
